IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg4-s204-ratification`
IMPORT `dg4-s205-validity`
IMPORT `dg4-s211-meetings`
IMPORT `dg4-s212-voting-proxies`
IMPORT `dg4-s213-record-dates`
IMPORT `dg4-s215-nonstock-members`
IMPORT `dg4-s216-quorum-vote`
IMPORT `dg4-s217-fiduciary-voting`
IMPORT `dg4-s218-voting-trusts`
IMPORT `dg4-s219-stockholder-list`
IMPORT `dg4-s220-inspection`
IMPORT `dg4-s220-court-orders`
IMPORT `dg4-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer dg4-seat.l4, one or more for every question, in the facts a person in the seat would state.
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text of the Law (de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, lines 671-889), beside each
-- assertion, never copied from the encoding's own output. People:
--   Alex Rivera, a minority stockholder of Acme Inc., a Delaware stock corporation;
--   Bea Chen, a director of Acme Inc.;
--   Cy Okafor, one of the persons who acted as the initial board of Acme Inc.;
--   Dee Park, a member of Park Commons, a Delaware nonprofit nonstock corporation.

§ `Cases for the seat: s 204 and s 205`

§§ `s 204(h): what is a defective corporate act, and what is my stock`

-- Case 1. Acme issued 1,200 shares of a class it could issue only 1,000 of. Alex asks whether that is a defective corporate act.
#ASSERT `Is the act a defective corporate act` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- An act of the corporation that is within its powers and void for a failure of authorization is one too; a lawful act is not.
#ASSERT `Is the act a defective corporate act` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the act a defective corporate act` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Case 2. The bylaws required board approval that was never given; that failure would make the act voidable.
#ASSERT `Is there a failure of authorization` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is there a failure of authorization` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is there a failure of authorization` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- Case 3. 1,200 shares purportedly issued, power to issue 1,000: an overissue. 900 of 1,000, in an authorized class: not.
#ASSERT `Is the issue of shares an overissue` 1200 1000 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the issue of shares an overissue` 900 1000 TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is the issue of shares an overissue` 10 1000 FALSE

-- Case 4. Alex's shares are validly issued shares of authorized capital stock: valid stock. Not if issuance was invalid.
#ASSERT `Are my shares valid stock` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my shares valid stock` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Case 5. Alex's shares would be valid but for a failure of authorization: putative stock. Shares nobody doubts are not.
#ASSERT `Are my shares putative stock` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my shares putative stock` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Case 6. The board judged Alex's shares valid; no fraud; no court determination: the board's judgment stands.
#ASSERT `Is the board's judgment on whether my shares are valid stock or putative stock conclusive` TRUE `shares that are valid stock under s 204(h)(7)` FALSE FALSE `shares that are putative stock under s 204(h)(4)` EQUALS JUST `shares that are valid stock under s 204(h)(7)`
-- Actual fraud: not conclusive.
#ASSERT `Is the board's judgment on whether my shares are valid stock or putative stock conclusive` TRUE `shares that are valid stock under s 204(h)(7)` TRUE FALSE `shares that are putative stock under s 204(h)(4)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Court of Chancery determined the shares are putative: that prevails.
#ASSERT `Is the board's judgment on whether my shares are valid stock or putative stock conclusive` TRUE `shares that are valid stock under s 204(h)(7)` FALSE TRUE `shares that are putative stock under s 204(h)(4)` EQUALS JUST `shares that are putative stock under s 204(h)(4)`

§§ `s 204(a) and (i): am I protected, and is s 204 the only way`

-- Case 7. Acme ratified the overissue under s 204: the issue is shielded. Nothing done: no shield from this section.
#ASSERT `Is the act or stock protected from being void or voidable solely for a failure of authorization` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the act or stock protected from being void or voidable solely for a failure of authorization` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the act or stock protected from being void or voidable solely for a failure of authorization` FALSE FALSE)

-- Case 8. Bea asks whether Acme must use s 204 or s 205: the Law keeps common-law and other means open.
#ASSERT `Is this a way the corporation may ratify or validate` `ratification under common law or otherwise`
#ASSERT `Is this a way the corporation may ratify or validate` `ratification under s 204`
#ASSERT `Is this a way the corporation may ratify or validate` `adoption or endorsement of an act taken in the name of the corporation before it began to exist`

-- Case 9. The act was properly ratified under common law: the lack of s 204 ratification does not of itself affect its validity.
#ASSERT `Does the lack of ratification of itself affect the validity of the act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the lack of ratification of itself affect the validity of the act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case 10. No s 204 ratification yet: no presumption that the act is defective.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the lack of ratification create a presumption that the act is defective` TRUE)

§§ `s 204(b) and (c): the board's resolutions and whether the stockholders must approve`

-- Case 11. Bea checks the resolutions: acts, dates, putative-stock details, nature of failure, approval.
#ASSERT `Do the board's resolutions state what section 204(b)(1) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Do the board's resolutions state what section 204(b)(1) requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the board's resolutions state what section 204(b)(1) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the board's resolutions state what section 204(b)(1) requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- Case 12. Acme's board has 7 directors. Now a quorum is 4 and 4 votes adopt. The bylaws at the time of the act needed a quorum of 6 and 5
-- votes, but one director of each count was elected by a series no longer outstanding: need 5 present and 4 votes. 5 present, 4 voting: adopted.
#ASSERT `Did the board adopt the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` 4 4 6 5 1 1 5 4
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the board adopt the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` 4 4 6 5 1 1 4 4)
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the board adopt the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` 4 4 6 5 1 0 5 4)

-- Case 13. The resolutions let the board abandon before the validation effective time of 10 March. Bea abandons on 5 March.
#ASSERT `May the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case 14. Cy and two others (3 of the 5 persons exercising the powers of directors) ratify the election of the initial board.
#ASSERT `May the persons exercising the powers of directors ratify the election of the initial board` TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the persons exercising the powers of directors ratify the election of the initial board` TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the persons exercising the powers of directors ratify the election of the initial board` TRUE TRUE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the persons exercising the powers of directors ratify the election of the initial board` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case 15. An overissue that failed s 203 needs the stockholders' approval; an act that nothing else required them to approve does not.
#ASSERT `Must the ratification be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the ratification be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the ratification be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the ratification be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `ratifying the election of the initial board of directors under s 204(b)(2)` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `s 204(d): the stockholders' meeting`

-- Case 16. Alex holds putative stock when notice is given: entitled. A former holder of record whose address is unknown: not.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to notice of the stockholders' meeting on the ratification` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to notice of the stockholders' meeting on the ratification` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to notice of the stockholders' meeting on the ratification` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to notice of the stockholders' meeting on the ratification` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Case 17. Notice given 1 March for a meeting on 21 March: 20 days. It states the time, the place and the purpose.
#ASSERT `Was notice of the meeting given in time and in full` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 21) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Was notice of the meeting given in time and in full` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was notice of the meeting given in time and in full` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 21) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

-- Case 18. The notice has the resolutions and the 120-day statement.
#ASSERT `Does the notice of the meeting contain what section 204(d)(3) requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the notice of the meeting contain what section 204(d)(3) requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Case 19. An ordinary act: quorum present and vote obtained.
#ASSERT `Did the stockholders approve the ratification` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The ratification of a director's election: 6 of 10 votes present is a majority; 5 of 10 is not.
#ASSERT `Did the stockholders approve the ratification` TRUE FALSE TRUE 6 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the stockholders approve the ratification` TRUE FALSE TRUE 5 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A failure to comply with s 203 also needs the s 203(a)(3) vote.
#ASSERT `Did the stockholders approve the ratification` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 10 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the stockholders approve the ratification` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 10 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A larger earlier requirement not met.
#ASSERT `Did the stockholders approve the ratification` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 10 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Counts that cannot be a vote for a director's ratification.
#ASSERT `Did the stockholders approve the ratification` TRUE FALSE TRUE 11 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case 20. Alex's shares were putative when the board adopted the resolutions: they neither vote nor count for a quorum.
#ASSERT `Can my putative shares vote on the ratification` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my putative shares vote on the ratification` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 204(e): the certificate of validation`

-- Case 21. Acme must file a certificate of validation where the act would have needed a s 103 certificate and none was filed.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation file a certificate of validation` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the corporation file a certificate of validation` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the corporation file a certificate of validation` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the corporation file a certificate of validation` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- Case 22. Two overissues of different classes may share one certificate; an overissue and an unrelated amendment may not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does each of several defective acts need its own certificate of validation` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Does each of several defective acts need its own certificate of validation` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does each of several defective acts need its own certificate of validation` TRUE FALSE)

-- Case 23. Overissues on 1 June 2025, 3 March 2024 and 9 January 2025: the increase takes effect as of the first, 3 March 2024.
#ASSERT `As of what date is the increase in authorized shares effective in a combined certificate` (LIST YearMonthDay 2025 6 1, YearMonthDay 2024 3 3, YearMonthDay 2025 1 9) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 3 3)

-- Case 24. A certificate where one was filed before and needs a change: name and filing date, attachment statement, effective date.
#ASSERT `Does the certificate of validation set forth what section 204(e)(3) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the certificate of validation set forth what section 204(e)(3) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Does the certificate of validation set forth what section 204(e)(3) requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE

-- Case 25. The certificate attached to a certificate of validation needs no separate execution or acknowledgment.
#ASSERT `Must the certificate attached to a certificate of validation be separately executed and acknowledged` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the certificate attached to a certificate of validation be separately executed and acknowledged` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 204(f) and (h)(6): when the ratification takes effect`

-- Case 26. A vote is required: stockholders approved 10 March; board adopted 1 March; no certificate; the board specified 15 March. The latest is 15 March.
#ASSERT `On what day is the validation effective time` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15)
-- With a certificate required and effective 20 March, the board's specified time is not a component: 20 March.
#ASSERT `On what day is the validation effective time` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 25) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20)
-- The stockholders have not yet voted: not determined.
#ASSERT `On what day is the validation effective time` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- No vote and no certificate: the day the board adopts the resolutions.
#ASSERT `On what day is the validation effective time` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)

-- Case 27. The act has been ratified when resolutions, board vote, stockholder approval and certificate are all in place.
#ASSERT `Has the defective corporate act been ratified in accordance with section 204` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the defective corporate act been ratified in accordance with section 204` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the defective corporate act been ratified in accordance with section 204` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Has the defective corporate act been ratified in accordance with section 204` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Case 28. After the validation effective time (10 March) the ratified act is no longer void or voidable: on 11 March yes, on 9 March no.
#ASSERT `Is the ratified act no longer void or voidable` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the ratified act no longer void or voidable` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the ratified act no longer void or voidable` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Case 29. The effect is retroactive to the date of the defective act, 4 July 2024.
#ASSERT `As of what date is the effect of the ratification retroactive` (YearMonthDay 2024 7 4) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2024 7 4

-- Case 30. Alex's putative share, issued under a ratified act, is an identical outstanding share after the validation effective time.
#ASSERT `Is my putative share now an identical outstanding share` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my putative share now an identical outstanding share` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Case 31. Alex's share was purportedly issued 15 January 2023: it is deemed outstanding as of then.
#ASSERT `As of what date is my putative share deemed outstanding` (YearMonthDay 2023 1 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2023 1 15

§§ `s 204(g): notice of the board's ratification`

-- Case 32. The board adopted the resolutions 1 March and set 30 April (within 60 days) as the notice date; 1 May would be too late.
#ASSERT `Is the day the board set for the notice record date permitted` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the day the board set for the notice record date permitted` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1))

-- Case 33. Alex holds putative stock on the notice date; no meeting notice is coming; the notice is not in a s 228(e) notice: owed.
#ASSERT `Am I owed notice of the board's ratification` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I owed notice of the board's ratification` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Alex consented in lieu of a meeting and the notice rides on a s 228(e) notice: not owed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I owed notice of the board's ratification` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- Case 34. Owed; not a listed corporation; Alex was given the notice promptly with the resolutions and the statement: done.
#ASSERT `Has the corporation done what section 204(g) requires for me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the corporation done what section 204(g) requires for me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- A listed corporation that disclosed it in an SEC filing: deemed given.
#ASSERT `Has the corporation done what section 204(g) requires for me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Case 35. Notice to Alex, a putative holder, for s 204(d) or (g): treated as notice to a holder of valid stock.
#ASSERT `Is the notice to me treated as notice to a holder of valid stock` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the notice to me treated as notice to a holder of valid stock` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the notice to me treated as notice to a holder of valid stock` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 205: the Court of Chancery`

-- Case 36. Alex holds putative stock: among those who may apply. A stranger to the corporation is not.
#ASSERT `Am I among those who may apply to the Court of Chancery under section 205` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I among those who may apply to the Court of Chancery under section 205` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I among those who may apply to the Court of Chancery under section 205` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- Case 37. Alex asks the Court to decide whether the ratification was effective, and whether any act not ratified is valid.
#ASSERT `What may the Court of Chancery determine on my application` `the validity and effectiveness of the ratification of a defective corporate act pursuant to s 204` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `What may the Court of Chancery determine on my application` `the validity and effectiveness of a defective corporate act not ratified or not ratified effectively pursuant to s 204` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`What may the Court of Chancery determine on my application` `the validity and effectiveness of a defective corporate act ratified pursuant to s 204` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Case 38. Validation effective time 1 March 2026; no notice required: the last day is 29 June 2026. Notice required, given 20 March: 18 July.
#ASSERT `By what day must I bring an action under section 205` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 29)
#ASSERT `By what day must I bring an action under section 205` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 7 18)
#ASSERT `By what day must I bring an action under section 205` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case 39. Alex's claim that a ratified issue is void for a failure of authorization, brought 30 June, is late; on 29 June it is not.
#ASSERT `Is my action barred by the 120-day limit` `a claim that a defective corporate act or putative stock ratified under s 204 is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization identified in the resolution adopted under s 204(b)` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 29) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my action barred by the 120-day limit` `a claim that a defective corporate act or putative stock ratified under s 204 is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization identified in the resolution adopted under s 204(b)` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 29) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 29))
-- Alex was owed notice and never got it: the limit does not apply to Alex.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my action barred by the 120-day limit` `a claim that a defective corporate act or putative stock ratified under s 204 is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization identified in the resolution adopted under s 204(b)` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 29) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1))
-- A claim that the ratification was not accomplished in accordance with s 204 is outside the limit.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my action barred by the 120-day limit` `a claim that a ratification was not accomplished in accordance with s 204` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 29) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1))

-- Case 40. Alex may apply and is not barred: may bring the action.
#ASSERT `May I bring the action` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I bring the action` TRUE TRUE)

-- Case 41. In Alex's action the Court may make the orders s 205(b) lists, once an action has been brought.
#ASSERT `May the Court of Chancery make this order in my action` `validation and a declaration of effect of a defective corporate act or putative stock, with conditions imposed by the Court` TRUE
#ASSERT `May the Court of Chancery make this order in my action` `approval of a stock ledger for the corporation that includes stock ratified or validated` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Court of Chancery make this order in my action` `such other orders regarding these matters as the Court deems proper under the circumstances` FALSE)

-- Case 42. Alex suffers a harm the ratification caused that would not have followed from a valid act: the Court may require measures.
#ASSERT `Is this harm harm the Court may require measures to remedy` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this harm harm the Court may require measures to remedy` TRUE TRUE)

-- Case 43. The Court orders an instrument filed; the filing date is the s 103(c)(3) date, 5 May 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the filing date of an instrument the Court orders filed` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 5) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 5

-- Case 44. Alex serves the registered agent: the corporation is deemed served.
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having served the corporation by serving its registered agent` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as having served the corporation by serving its registered agent` FALSE)

-- Case 45. No other party need be joined.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must I join another party for the Court of Chancery to decide my application` TRUE)

-- Case 46. In the corporation's own action the Court may require notice to others and let them intervene.
#ASSERT `May the Court of Chancery require notice of the corporation's action to other persons` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the Court of Chancery require notice of the corporation's action to other persons` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case 47. The Court may weigh whether anyone relied on the public record that the act was valid.
#ASSERT `May the Court of Chancery consider this factor` `whether the corporation and its board of directors have treated the defective corporate act as valid, and whether any person has acted in reliance on the public record that it was valid` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Court of Chancery consider this factor` `any other factor the Court deems just and equitable` FALSE)

-- Case 48. Harm that would have followed anyway from a valid act is not harm the Court considers.
#ASSERT `Is the harm to me harm the Court considers` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the harm to me harm the Court considers` TRUE TRUE)

-- Case 49. Only the Court of Chancery has jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `Does the Court of Chancery have jurisdiction over my action under section 205` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the Court of Chancery have jurisdiction over my action under section 205` FALSE)

§ `Cases for the seat: s 211`

-- Case 50. Acme's bylaws say where meetings are held: the bylaws decide. With no designation the board decides.
#ASSERT `Who decides where the stockholders' meeting is held` TRUE EQUALS `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws, by designation or in the manner they provide`
#ASSERT `Who decides where the stockholders' meeting is held` FALSE EQUALS `the board of directors`

-- Case 51. Nothing designated in the certificate or bylaws: the board may go remote-only. Designated and no authority: it may not.
#ASSERT `May the board decide the meeting is held solely by remote communication` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the board decide the meeting is held solely by remote communication` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the board decide the meeting is held solely by remote communication` TRUE TRUE

-- Case 52. The board authorized remote participation and Alex follows its guidelines: Alex may take part.
#ASSERT `May I take part in the meeting by remote communication` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I take part in the meeting by remote communication` FALSE TRUE)

-- Case 53. Alex may take part, and Acme verifies identity, gives a reasonable opportunity to take part and keeps a record: deemed present, may vote.
#ASSERT `Am I deemed present in person and may I vote by remote communication` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I deemed present in person and may I vote by remote communication` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Case 54. Acme (a stock corporation) must hold an annual meeting unless directors are elected by consent in lieu. A nonstock corporation: s 211(b) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation hold an annual meeting for the election of directors` `a stock corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the corporation hold an annual meeting for the election of directors` `a stock corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the corporation hold an annual meeting for the election of directors` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case 55. The bylaws designate the date and time.
#ASSERT `Are the date and time of the annual meeting designated as required` `a stock corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the date and time of the annual meeting designated as required` `a stock corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Case 56. Acme's certificate says nothing against consents: stockholders may act by written consent to elect directors.
#ASSERT `May the stockholders act by written consent to elect directors` `a stock corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the stockholders act by written consent to elect directors` `a stock corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Case 57. A consent that is not unanimous takes the place of the annual meeting only if all directorships are vacant and filled by it.
#ASSERT `Does a written consent take the place of the annual meeting` `a stock corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a written consent take the place of the annual meeting` `a stock corporation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a written consent take the place of the annual meeting` `a stock corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Case 58. Other proper business may be transacted at the annual meeting.
#ASSERT `May other proper business be transacted at the annual meeting` `a stock corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Case 59. Acme missed its annual meeting; the Law does not specifically say that works a forfeiture.
#ASSERT `Does the failure to hold the annual meeting affect corporate acts or work a forfeiture` `a stock corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the failure to hold the annual meeting affect corporate acts or work a forfeiture` `a stock corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Case 60. The annual meeting was not held on its date and no consent was taken: the directors must cause it to be held.
#ASSERT `Must the directors cause the annual meeting to be held` `a stock corporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the directors cause the annual meeting to be held` `a stock corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Case 61. Bea, a director, applies on 31 January 2026; the meeting was due 1 January 2026 (30 days later is 31 January).
#ASSERT `May I ask the Court of Chancery to order the annual meeting` `a stock corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I ask the Court of Chancery to order the annual meeting` `a stock corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 30) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No date designated: 13 months after the latest of organization (31 Aug 2024), last meeting (15 Jan 2025) and last consent (1 Mar 2025): 1 April 2026.
#ASSERT `May I ask the Court of Chancery to order the annual meeting` `a stock corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 8 31) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I ask the Court of Chancery to order the annual meeting` `a stock corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 8 31) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Park Commons (nonstock): s 211(c) does not apply.
#ASSERT `May I ask the Court of Chancery to order the annual meeting` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case 62. At the meeting the Court ordered, 40 shares are represented: they are a quorum.
#ASSERT `Do the shares represented at the court-ordered meeting form a quorum` `a stock corporation` 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do the shares represented at the court-ordered meeting form a quorum` `a stock corporation` 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Case 63. The Court may order the time and place of the meeting it ordered.
